[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Tilting the controller moves the pointer, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}.
The right stick {rs} moves the cursor, which is where you aim, and what you point at is what you use. {rt} uses the item in your hands: fire, weld, repair, cut. {lt} aims a weapon or tool.
{ls} walks, climbs ladders and swims; a full push runs (Shift). Click {l3} to crouch, and again to stand.
{south} interacts with what you point at (E): doors, terminals, the helm, a crewmate. {east} grabs and drags a body (G). {west} opens the health screen (H), {north} the crew and missions list (Tab).
{lb} opens the command interface to give orders (Q), and clicking {r3} gives a quick order for what you point at (middle mouse). Hold {rb} for the hotbar and pick a slot with {rs}; {up} and {down} turn the wheel.
{left} and {right} switch to the previous and next crewmate in single player. {select} lists chat, radio chat and ragdoll. {start} opens the menu (Escape).
Chat needs typing: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard.
The keys are remembered defaults, unchecked on an install; the command interface, grab and crew-switch keys are the least sure. If one doesn't answer, check Settings → Controls and change the pack to match.'''

